       "  '43.9 Stress tests (applied to the FY28 bank case)\\nMild: DSCR ≥ 1.10x, As requested = 1.04x ✘ fail. Mild: DSCR ≥ 1.10x, As recommended = 1.12x ✔ pass (thin). Moderate: DSCR ≥ 1.00x or runway ≥ 12 months, As requested = 0.60x and 9 months ✘ fail. Moderate: DSCR ≥ 1.00x or runway ≥ 12 months, As recommended = Runway 24 months ✔ pass. Severe: runway ≥ 6 months and forced-sale security cover ≥ 80%, As requested = 5 months ✘ fail; cover 111%. Severe: runway ≥ 6 months and forced-sale security cover ≥ 80%, As recommended = 12 months ✔; cover 121% ✔. Mild stress breaches a covenant in first 12 months?, As requested = n/a. Mild stress breaches a covenant in first 12 months?, As recommended = No (mild DSCR 1.12x vs covenant 1.10x)\\nSector stress (food manufacturing, Section 14.4). Loss of Customer A over 6 months removes c. £6.4m of bank-case revenue post-expansion. No structure survives this on cash flow, which is why contract terms and concentration monitoring matter more than leverage here. Under the recommended structure, committed liquidity of £450k and security cover of 121% in the severe case give Northbridge time and a low expected loss if it occurs.',\n",
