       "  '43.11 Risk grade, PD and return\\n| - |\\n| Cash flow and debt service, Key input = Pro-forma DSCR 1.28x; CFO / debt. Cash flow and debt service, Points = 56. Cash flow and debt service, Max = 90. Leverage, Key input = Pro-forma net debt / EBITDA 2.05x; gearing. Leverage, Points = 50. Leverage, Max = 72. Account conduct, Key input = Average OD utilisation 55%; no excesses or returns. Account conduct, Points = 62. Account conduct, Max = 72. Credit bureau, Key input = Clean; pays 3 days beyond terms on average. Credit bureau, Points = 50. Credit bureau, Max = 60. Liquidity, Key input = Current 1.39x; quick 0.91x. Liquidity, Points = 34. Liquidity, Max = 48. Profitability, Key input = EBITDA margin 10.4%. Profitability, Points = 28. Profitability, Max = 48. Industry risk, Key input = Sector score 3. Industry risk, Points = 24. Industry risk, Max = 48. Business performance, Key input = Revenue CAGR 7.4%; EBITDA margin -2.1pp over 2 years. Business performance, Points = 18. Business performance, Max = 42. Management quality, Key input = Experience strong; succession weak. Management quality, Points = 28. Management quality, Max = 42. Customer relationship, Key input = Banked 12 years. Customer relationship, Points = 26. Customer relationship, Max = 30. Business model / concentration, Key input = Largest customer 45% post-expansion. Business model / concentration, Points = 6. Business model / concentration, Max = 30. External environment, Key input = Energy and labour sensitivity. External environment, Points = 8. External environment, Max = 18. Category points + 250 base',\n",
       "  '43.11 Risk grade, PD and return\\n| - |\\n points, Key input = . Category points + 250 base points, Points = 640. Category points + 250 base points, Max = 850 |\\n\\nScore 640 → odds 100:1 → model PD 0.99% → grade 6 (score band 612-651). No qualitative adjustment: concentration and margin trend are already scored. Master Scale central PD of 1.20% is used for EL and pricing.\\nPD, Value = 1.20%. LGD, Value = 28% (first-charge property plus debenture). EAD, Value = £2.71m = TLs £2.35m + RCF drawn £150k + 60% CCF × £350k undrawn. Expected loss, Value = 1.20% × 28% × £2.71m = c.£9.1k a year. Pricing, Value = TL SONIA + 3.00%; RCF SONIA + 3.50% plus 0.75% non-utilisation fee; arrangement fee 1.25% (above grade-6 minimum margin of 2.50%). RAROC (illustrative), Value = 16.5%, above the 14% hurdle',\n",
       "  '43.12 Key risks and mitigants\\n| - |\\n| Margin erosion: gross margin down 3pp in 2 years under grocer pricing pressure and input inflation, Mitigant = Bank case assumes no recovery; YTD margin stable at 10.6%; stress- tested; gross-margin EWI at 26%. Margin erosion: gross margin down 3pp in 2 years under grocer pricing pressure and input inflation, Residual = Moderate. Customer concentration: Customer A rises from 38% to c.45% of revenue, Mitigant = 3-year signed supply agreement as CP; termination-notice covenant; concentration EWI at 50%; recommended debt serviceable without the new volume. Customer concentration: Customer A rises from 38% to c.45% of revenue, Residual = Moderate - accepted. Execution: commissioning delay or cost overrun, Mitigant = Fixed-price installation contract with supplier performance retention; 6- month interest-only period; staged drawdown paid directly to supplier; £350k undrawn RCF. Execution: commissioning delay or cost overrun, Residual = Low. Forecast risk on incremental volume, Mitigant = 40% haircut; recommended structure passes 1.25x on historical cash flow. Forecast risk on incremental volume, Residual = Low. Key person and succession: founder MD aged 61, no plan, Mitigant = Key-person cover (CS); succession plan (CS); capable Operations Director. Key person and succession: founder MD aged 61, no plan, Residual = Moderate. Cost shocks: energy (fixed until Sept 2027) and wages, Mitigant = Stress-tested; energy-renewal EWI. Cost shocks: energy (fixed until Sept 2027) and wages, Residual = Moderate. Interest rate: c.70% of debt floating after drawdown, Mitigant = Stress-tested at +500bps; hedging for 50% of the',\n",
