       "  '43.13 Independent challenge log (extract)\\n1, Credit challenge = Why not use the management case, given the letter of intent?. 1, RM / customer response = LOI only; agreement expected in Q4 2026. 1, Outcome = Policy 40% haircut applied; signed agreement made a CP\\n2, Credit challenge = Customer A moved to 60- day terms in FY26: a sign of buyer power?. 2, RM / customer response = Confirmed; part of a supplier-wide change. 2, Outcome = Reflected in CCC and ΔWC; debtor-days EWI at 65. 3, Credit challenge = Requested structure fails mild stress. Fix by extending tenor to 10 years?. 3, RM / customer response = RM proposed 10 years. 3, Outcome = Rejected: specialist food equipment faces technology and hygiene- standard change; 7.5 years is the prudent economic life for lending. Owner contribution preferred. 4, Credit challenge = Is a personal guarantee needed?. 4, RM / customer response = MD contributing £500k subordinated. 4, Outcome = Not required: unsecured exposure nil, grade 6, no Section 17.1 trigger; owner alignment achieved through subordinated funds',\n",
       "  '43.14 Recommended facilities and terms\\nTerm loan B (new, capex), Amount = £1,750,000. Term loan B (new, capex), Tenor and repayment = 7.5 years: 6 months interest-only, then 84 monthly amortising instalments. Term loan B (new, capex), Pricing = SONIA + 3.00%. RCF (new), Amount = £500,000. RCF (new), Tenor and repayment = 3 years committed. RCF (new), Pricing = SONIA + 3.50%; 0.75% non-utilisation fee. Term loan A (existing), Amount = £600,000. Term loan A (existing), Tenor and repayment = Unchanged: 5 years remaining. Term loan A (existing), Pricing = Fixed 6.50%. Overdraft (existing), Amount = £300,000. Overdraft (existing), Tenor and repayment = Cancelled on RCF drawdown. Overdraft (existing), Pricing = -. TCE, Amount = £2,850,000. TCE, Tenor and repayment = . TCE, Pricing = \\nSecurity: new all-monies debenture (fixed and floating charges), replacing the existing debenture; existing first legal charge over the freehold factory extended to all monies; fixed charge over the new production line; deed of postponement over the £500k director loan. No personal guarantee.',\n",
       "  'Financial covenants (quarterly, LTM, from 30 September 2027)\\nDSCR, Level = ≥ 1.10x, stepping to ≥ 1.20x from 31 March 2029. DSCR, Bank case at first test = c.1.45x. DSCR, Headroom = 24%. Senior net debt / Normalised EBITDA, Level = ≤ 2.50x. Senior net debt / Normalised EBITDA, Bank case at first test = c.1.90x. Senior net debt / Normalised EBITDA, Headroom = 24%\\nNon-financial covenants: standard package (Section 18.2), plus: distributions capped at £100k a year to 31 March 2029, and only if post-distribution DSCR ≥ 1.35x and leverage ≤ 2.0x; no repayment of the director loan while Term loan B is outstanding without Credit consent; non-project capex ≤ £350k a year; notice within 5 working days of any termination notice or volume reduction > 15% from Customer A.',\n",
       "  \"Conditions precedent\\n1. Signed supply agreement with Customer A for the premium range: term ≥ 3 years; volumes ≥ 70% of the management case.\\n2. £500k director loan received in the company's Northbridge account, with deed of postponement executed and source of funds verified.\\n3. Company cash contribution of £150k paid to the supplier, evidenced.\\n4. Fixed-price supply and installation contract with the equipment supplier, including commissioning performance retention of at least 10%.\\n5. Security documents executed and registered; Companies House and Land Registry registrations confirmed.\\n6. Specialist valuation of the new production line from a panel valuer.\\n7. Buildings, plant and business-interruption insurance (≥ 12 months) with Northbridge noted as loss payee.\\n8. Drawdowns of Term loan B paid directly to the supplier in three stages (30% order, 60% delivery, 10% commissioning).\",\n",
       "  'Conditions subsequent\\n1. Key-person life and critical-illness cover on the MD for £500k, assigned to Northbridge, within 60 days.\\n2. Commissioning certificate within 9 months of first drawdown.\\n3. Board-approved succession plan within 6 months.',\n",
       "  'Monitoring plan\\n- Monthly management accounts within 30 days for 12 months from drawdown, then quarterly.\\n- Quarterly covenant compliance certificate, aged debtors and customer-concentration report.\\n- Monthly commissioning-progress report until the line is commissioned.\\n- Semi-annual desk review (next: 31 March 2027); full annual review by 30 September 2027.\\n- Obligor-specific EWIs: Customer A > 50% of revenue; quarterly gross margin < 26%; debtor days > 65; commissioning delay > 3 months or overrun > 10%; energy contract unhedged 3 months before September 2027 expiry.',\n",
       "  '43.15 Final credit decision\\nDecline the facilities as requested. The £2.0m term loan with £500k RCF, funded almost entirely by debt, fails the mild stress (DSCR 1.04x vs 1.10x) and the moderate and severe liquidity tests. Under Section 14.2 these failures require decline or restructure; no exception route exists for a mild-stress failure.\\nApprove the amended structure set out in Section 43.14, subject to the CPs, at grade 6, within L5 authority. The decision rests on: historical cash flow covering the new debt service at 1.28x without relying on the new contract; senior leverage of 2.05x; committed liquidity sufficient for 24 months of the moderate-stress shortfall; and 132% security cover. The main accepted risk is customer concentration, managed through the CP, covenants and EWIs rather than avoided.\\nRecommended by, Detail = Relationship Director, Midlands Commercial (amended recommendation). Independent challenge, Detail = Credit Manager, Midlands Commercial Credit. Approved by, Detail = Senior Credit Manager (L5), jointly with Commercial Manager (L2). Decision, Detail = Approve with amendments. Approval valid to, Detail = 90 days from approval\\nNext review, Detail = Semi-annual desk review 31 March 2027; annual review 30 September 2027'],\n",
